  "label": "Repetitive Affection Stereotype",
  "description": "The phrase 'husband husband you are my husband' plays on the trope of exaggerated or performative declarations of love and devotion, often used humorously or ironically in memes and social media to express over-the-top affection. This trope is common in internet culture and relies on the understanding of how people express romantic or marital devotion in a comically redundant way.",
